Pat wants to know that beastie's mail client works before he switches
Emacs to lab-mail. The client check in dotfiles/notmuch covers what
every host shares, but not what is beastie's own: its configs could
be missing or edited since just install-mail, the password file
empty or readable by others, or a port not installed. Any of these
would show up only as a failed sync after the switch.

just check-mail checks those, then runs the client check, so one
command answers whether beastie is ready. Like the client check, it
prints one ok or FAIL line per check and changes nothing.
